					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13133120#post-4611628</guid>
				<title>Re: minor nitpick</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13133120/a-dark-green-kiss#post-4611628</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2020 01:53:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dyslexion</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5549954</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The frisbee line is a reference to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5023">SCP-5023</a>, my entry to the first Jamcon prompt. This is the only draft of this to exist, as it was written directly on the wiki and received no critique prior to posting.</p> <p>The difference between the main character’s infection and everyone else’s is direct contact. It’s like how in a zombie movie, you can catch the virus and succumb over several days or weeks, or get bitten and turn really quickly. Except, of course, you’re the one eating the zombie.</p> <p>From a virology point of view, the remains of a consumed M&amp;M would be a pretty dangerous vector of transmission, as dogs, cats, bird, and rats could all track pieces of compromised chocolate into homes and public spaces. This is what’s happening to the other people.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
